---
// Phase 6 — the transcript result surface.
//
// Kept as its own file, exactly as AudioResult.astro is: this is the only
// place this markup exists. SttPanel clones the <template> below and fills the
// data slots, so the structure is authored in Astro (styled and type-checked
// like everything else) while the values arrive from the response at runtime.
// Two copies of this markup would drift.
//
// DESIGN.md shapes:
//   `components.feature-card` for the surface — white, 1px hairline,
//     rounded.md (12px) → rounded-card, body-md type, padding {spacing.lg}
//     24px. A hairline card inside the panel's own card gives the depth step
//     the system wants (Level 0 flat → Level 1 whisper) with no second shadow.
//   `components.button-primary` for Copy — ink fill, white label, rounded.pill
//     (100px), padding 0 14px, {typography.button-lg} 16/20.
//   `components.button-ghost-sm` for the raw-transcript disclosure — a 6px
//     square, hairline, body-md. DESIGN.md: the 6px square and the circular
//     mic button are never mixed within one context, and the mic lives in the
//     panel header, not in this result card.
//   `components.mono-eyebrow` for the "Transcript" label — Geist Mono, 12/16,
//     uppercase, {colors.mute}.
//
// Note what is deliberately absent: the pill shape is used for the single
// primary action (Copy) and the ghost square for the secondary disclosure.
// That is the one place both shapes are adjacent, and they are not mixed
// within a single control — the ordering matches DESIGN.md's own rule that
// the mic control is circular and panel controls are 6px squares.
//
---

<div id="stt-result" class="mt-6"></div>

<template id="stt-transcript">
	<div class="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-card border border-hairline bg-elevated p-6 shadow-whisper">
		<p class="font-mono text-xs leading-4 font-medium tracking-normal text-mute uppercase">
			Transcript
		</p>

		<!--
			The provisional live draft and the authoritative transcript are the
			same box, in two states. Interim text renders in {colors.mute} so it
			reads as provisional; the final text renders in {colors.ink}. The
			distinction is carried by colour and by the live-region label, not
			by swapping in different elements — which would move focus and lose
			the announcement.

			PHASE 5.4: `lang` starts as `en` and is rewritten from the
			transcription's own language by SttPanel. The page is `lang="en"`,
			so a Bengali or Devanagari transcript was being announced with
			English phonetics — a screen reader reads a Bengali ল as an
			English "ell", which makes a correct transcript sound like gibberish.
			The attribute is the entire fix, and it exists for precisely this.
			`en` rather than absent as the initial value, because a live draft
			arrives before any language is known.
		-->
		<div data-role="surface" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" class="min-h-16">
			<p data-role="text" lang="en" class="text-sm leading-5 whitespace-pre-wrap text-mute"></p>
		</div>

		<p data-role="status" class="hidden text-xs leading-4 text-mute"></p>

		<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
			<!-- Primary. Only rendered once a transcript actually exists;
			     SttPanel adds/removes `hidden`. -->
			<button
				data-role="copy"
				type="button"
				class="hidden cursor-pointer rounded-pill bg-ink px-3.5 py-1 text-base leading-5 font-medium text-on-primary"
			>
				Copy transcript
			</button>
			<p data-role="copied" class="hidden text-xs leading-4 text-mute">Copied to clipboard</p>
		</div>

		<!-- 6.6 — the raw-transcript disclosure. A <details> element is used
		     rather than a scripted toggle: it is keyboard accessible and works
		     with no JavaScript at all, and the panel's own state is what
		     needs scripting, not this. -->
		<details data-role="raw-details" class="hidden rounded-app border border-hairline bg-hairline-soft p-4">
			<summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm leading-5 font-medium text-ink">
				Show raw transcript
			</summary>
			<!-- `lang` is kept in step with the transcript above, for the same
			     reason: a raw disclosure is read just as often, and it is read
			     in the same language. -->
			<p
				data-role="raw"
				lang="en"
				class="mt-3 text-sm leading-5 whitespace-pre-wrap text-body"
			></p>
		</details>
	</div>
</template>
